# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build
build/
install/
log/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ------------------------------------------------------- python environments
# .kortex_venv holds the Kinova kortex_api wheel, which pins protobuf 3.5.1
# and must stay isolated from the protobuf ROS needs. Rebuild it with the
# recipe in README.md; do not commit it.
.kortex_venv/
# .percep_venv is 5.6 GB: torch, CUDA runtime libraries, faster-whisper and
# ultralytics. Nothing in it is ours.
.percep_venv/
# .venv_vision is 1.4 GB: torch, ultralytics, opencv and pyrealsense2. It is
# built with --system-site-packages so rclpy stays visible, which is why the
# vision scripts and the ROS nodes can run in one process. Nothing in it is
# ours; rebuild it rather than commit it.
.venv_vision/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ model weights
# Downloaded on first use, not authored here, and one of them is larger than
# GitHub's 100 MB hard limit:
#   weights/clip/ViT-B-32.pt   337.6 MB   CLIP text encoder, pulled by
#                                         ultralytics when YOLO-World's
#                                         set_classes() is first called
#   yolov8s-worldv2.pt          24.7 MB   YOLO-World detector
# Both reappear automatically; see README.md.
weights/
*.pt
*.onnx
*.engine

# ----------------------------------------------------------- vendor packages
# Cloned, not authored. Patches that must be applied to them live in patches/
# and ARE tracked. See README.md for the clone commands.
src/ros2_kortex/
src/ros2_robotiq_gripper/
src/ros2_kortex_vision/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ scratch
*.log
core
/tmp/

# ------------------------------------------------- verification recordings
# recordings/verification/ holds one rosbag2 per task x scenario x condition
# (~87 of them). The CLIPS, PLOTS and summaries are tracked -- they are the
# reviewable artefact and are small. The BAGS are not: they are regenerable
# from the same script in one command and would dominate the repo.
extras/recordings/verification/*/*/*/bag/

# ---------------------------------------------- per-angle verification rushes
# Each run records seven camera angles. rviz_quad.mp4 tiles the four that
# matter and is what anyone actually reviews, so only the quad is tracked; the
# individual angles are ~950 MB in total and regenerate in one command via
# scripts/record_rviz.py. Several were also left unfinalised by an interrupted
# sweep and cannot be stream-copied back to a sane size.
#
# THE FIVE-TASK CLIPS (f1..f5) KEEP EVERY ANGLE. They are recompressed at
# crf 30 -- 266 files, 132 MB, largest 5.3 MB -- which is small enough to
# track, and a single angle cannot answer every question: the front view
# flattens reach depth, the top view is where a coordination error shows, and
# only the gripper view answers "did it actually close on it".
#
# The retired nine-task clips (t2..t9) keep only the quad tile, because that
# sweep was interrupted mid-encode and its rushes cannot be stream-copied back
# to a sane size.
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_front.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_back.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_left.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_right.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_iso.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_top.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_side.mp4
extras/recordings/verification/t?/*/*/rviz_gripper.mp4

# RViz's own per-view log files, written beside each clip during a sweep.
# They are transient stderr, not evidence, and they churn on every run.
extras/recordings/verification/**/rviz.rviz.*
extras/recordings/verification/**/*.xvfb
.cad_venv/
datasets/

# ------------------------------------------ ARCHIVED verification recordings
# archive/recordings/verification_<date>/ is the SUPERSEDED sweep, moved under
# the standing never-delete rule. Moving it silently took it OUT of the rules
# above -- which is how a directory of bags nearly landed in a commit -- so
# those rules are MIRRORED here rather than replaced by a blanket ignore.
#
# WHY THE CLIPS STAY TRACKED. A rename adds no new blob: git stores by content
# hash, so re-pointing 612 already-tracked mp4 costs the repository nothing.
# Ignoring them instead would leave the archive on MY disk only, and a
# collaborator cloning the repo would find a GEOMETRY_NOTE.md citing evidence
# that is not there. That is deletion with extra steps.
extras/archive/recordings/*/*/*/*/bag/
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_front.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_back.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_left.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_right.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_iso.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_top.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_side.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/*/t?/*/*/rviz_gripper.mp4
extras/archive/recordings/**/rviz.rviz.*
extras/archive/recordings/**/*.xvfb

# ------------------------------------------------------- the pose interpreter
# .venv_pose holds MediaPipe, which pulls numpy 2.x and cannot be installed
# system-wide without breaking the scipy and matplotlib every analysis script
# in this repository uses. It is rebuilt by scripts/run_wearer_tracker.sh,
# which prints the two pip lines and why their ORDER matters.
.venv_pose/
# .venv_lerobot holds huggingface lerobot, which requires numpy>=2.0 and
# torch 2.11+cu130. It is SEPARATE from .venv_vision on purpose: installing
# lerobot there upgraded numpy to 2.2.6, broke the system scipy that
# scripts/real_calibration/ depends on, and took check_all.py from 4 of 4
# passing to 2 of 4. Rebuild with `python3 -m venv .venv_lerobot &&
# .venv_lerobot/bin/pip install "lerobot[dataset]"`; do not commit it and do
# not install lerobot into any other environment. See docs/system/20_lerobot.md
.venv_lerobot/

# The pose model bundles: ~23 MB of binary that is fetched, not authored.
# scripts/run_wearer_tracker.sh prints the one curl line.
models/mediapipe/

# Rehearsal calibrations live here and are NOMINAL, NOT MEASURED. They must
# never be mistaken for a calibration of a real camera, so they never leave
# scratch and they never enter config/.
.scratch/

# Regenerated by every calibration run, 1.1 MB of points. `pick_from_map`
# says plainly when it is absent rather than planning as though the table
# were not there.
extras/recordings/baselines/*_occupancy.npy
extras/recordings/calibration/*/world_map_occupancy.npy
# The scene camera's reference frame: a raw image, regenerated by pressing
# SET REFERENCE, and meaningless on a machine with a different camera.
extras/recordings/baselines/scene_reference.npz

# derived: one PNG per slide, regenerable by scripts/preview_presentation.py
# (contact_sheet.png IS committed -- it is the "look at it" artefact)
extras/presentation/preview/slide_*.png
extras/presentation/.build/

# ------------------------------------------------- session recordings
# `recordings/sessions/*/bag/` holds one rosbag2 per RECORD EVERYTHING
# session. They are multi-gigabyte .mcap files -- one 4.3 second recording
# reached 12 GB before 2026-08-30, when the recorder still captured
# UNCOMPRESSED camera frames at 1121 MB/s -- and GitHub refuses any file over
# 100 MB. The analysis beside them is small and IS tracked: trail.csv,
# summary.json, events.jsonl, manifest.json, arms.jsonl and the figures.
# `docs/RECORDINGS.md` indexes every session so the bags are not needed to
# see what was captured.
extras/recordings/sessions/*/bag/
extras/recordings/vr_teleop/*/*.mcap

# ------------------------------------------------------- participant sessions
# recordings/sessions/ is 129 GB of pilot recordings and its folder names
# were typed at the console, so they can carry a participant's name. Never
# commit it: anonymity is enforced in code and this keeps it enforced in git.
# The derived, anonymised session tables live in thesis_v3/figures/pilot/data/.
extras/recordings/sessions/

# --------------------------------------------------------- local-only files
# The engineering log lives at docs/ENGINEERING_LOG.md; the root-level
# CLAUDE.md is a local symlink to it for the coding assistant and is not
# tracked, and neither is the assistant's own state directory.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.scratch/
.cad_venv/
